--TEST--
An event stream's payload becomes `data:` lines and reaches no other field, whichever of the three line endings it carries — `rule:concurrency/a-stream-that-outlives-its-request-is-a-connection` and `rule:security/sink-predicate`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A client ends a line on `\n`, on `\r\n` and on `\r` alike, and the last of
// those is the one a program reaches by accident -- a Windows file read in, a
// spreadsheet's export. Every payload is normalized and then split, one `data:`
// line per line, so the three spellings frame identically and a caller never
// has to know which one it is holding.
var $lf = Core\Out::capture(fn (): void => {
    var $sse = Core\Sse::stream();
    $sse->send("first\nsecond");
});
var $cr = Core\Out::capture(fn (): void => {
    var $sse = Core\Sse::stream();
    $sse->send("first\rsecond");
});
var $crlf = Core\Out::capture(fn (): void => {
    var $sse = Core\Sse::stream();
    $sse->send("first\r\nsecond");
});
// Interpolated rather than compared as they came back: `Core\Out::capture`
// answers the sink's carrier, and two carriers are two objects.
var $written = "{$lf}";
echo $written;
echo $written == "{$cr}" ? "a lone carriage return agrees\n" : "a lone carriage return frames differently\n";
echo $written == "{$crlf}" ? "a carriage return and line feed agrees\n" : "a carriage return and line feed frames differently\n";
echo "--\n";

// This is what makes `$data` admit a `tainted` value: the framing belongs to
// the framer, so a payload that spells a field of its own is one event with a
// two-line payload and never a second event naming itself.
var $forged = Core\Out::capture(fn (): void => {
    var $sse = Core\Sse::stream();
    $sse->send("harmless\nevent: admin\nid: 9");
});
echo $forged;
echo "--\n";

// A payload ending in a line break keeps it: a client appends each data line
// and a `\n` to its buffer and strips one `\n` at dispatch, so the trailing
// empty line is what makes the round trip exact rather than merely safe.
var $trailing = Core\Out::capture(fn (): void => {
    var $sse = Core\Sse::stream();
    $sse->send("line\n");
});
echo $trailing;
echo "--\n";
--EXPECT--
data: first
data: second

a lone carriage return agrees
a carriage return and line feed agrees
--
data: harmless
data: event: admin
data: id: 9

--
data: line
data:

--
